request: In the watchlist, show movies I haven't watched yet before the ones I've watched.

governor turn 1: plan -> watchlist  (The request only changes the order in which the watchlist view displays items. That is entirely a presentation concern inside the watchlist unit; the store's stored order and all other units are unaffected, so no interface changes are needed. An acceptance test pins the unwatched-first partition and its reactivity.)
round 1: owners watchlist=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist  (The owner's implementation was correct; the only blocker was two existing tests that re-queried the first row after toggling — under the new display order that row legitimately changes, and the proposed edits preserve each test's intent (clicking the checkbox / blank row area toggles watched for that movie) while only fixing the element query, which the request's reordering genuinely requires. I approve both edits and re-issue the same plan. Separately, the NG0201 failure was in my acceptance-test harness (missing router providers for the template's routerLink), not in any unit; I am replacing that acceptance test with a corrected version.)
round 2: owners watchlist=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 3: accept  (Oracle is green (31 tests, 0 failed) and the acceptance tests confirm the request: the watchlist view now partitions items stably — unwatched movies first, watched after — and reorders immediately when a movie's watched status is toggled. The two approved test edits were applied by the owner and all other existing behaviour is unchanged.)

